<title>JORDAN: Jordan's June trade deficit narrows slightly.</title>
<headline>Jordan's June trade deficit narrows slightly.</headline>
<dateline>AMMAN 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jordan's trade deficit narrowed marginally in June to 180.3 million dinars ($254.6 million) from 181.2 million in May, Central Bank statistics received by Reuters on Thursday showed.</p>
<p>But the June deficit was sharply up from 149.2 million dinars in the same month last year:</p>
<p>(All figures in millions of dinars)</p>
<p>			 June 96    May 96  June 95    1995   1994</p>
<p>Domestic Exports	98.1	76.2     86.6   1,004    794</p>
<p>Re-Exports		23.1	21.4     17.7     237    201</p>
<p>Imports		  301.5     278.8    253.5   2,590  2,363</p>
<p>Trade balance	 -180.3    -181.2   -149.2  -1,349 -1,368</p>
<p>- Amman newsroom 9626 623 776</p>
</text>
